  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Forsah&quot; Technical and Vocational Education Training (TVET) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(West Bank and Gaza):  .USAID launched the Forsah TVET Activity in October 2022 and will work with approximately 12 TVET institutions across the West Bank, Gaza and East Jerusalem, to improve their performance, make their facilities accessible and green, and develop relationships between the TVET institutions and the private sector. The participating TVET institutions will sustainably respond to and predict workforce demand and will adapt their programs to meet the labor market needs. Moreover, the activity will green skills to enable youth to consider the effects of climate change and introduce mitigation and adaptation measures in the industrial/service sector in which they will be working. The activity will also work with the TVET institutions and youth to launch awareness campaigns, and award scholarships to marginalized youth to encourage them to enroll in approximately 16 new/modernized training programs taught by highly qualified instructors. USAID will also work on facilitating girl&apos;s enrollment in TVET programs and promoting female leaders at the TVET institutions..Using FY22 funds, the activity will work with the targeted TVET institutions on improving management capacity, updating/developing new market-driven training programs, and renovating/expanding the facilities of the TVET institutions to accommodate new training programs and make them accessible for people with disabilities. Funds will also support efforts to forge linkages between the TVET institutions and relevant private sector firms, providing apprenticeship opportunities for the TVET students and facilitating the enrollment of girls in TVET training programs. .This activity will contribute to Higher Education earmark..</narrative>
  </description>
